  "$comment": "How a genius is assembled: its body (one per silhouette) and parts (one per feature) on named sockets. When the art exists, the body is game/assets/genius/bodies/<silhouette>.glb with empties named socket_<name>, and each part is game/assets/genius/parts/<feature>.glb; the game uses them and ignores the placeholders below. Placeholder bodies are built from a kind: quadruped and humanoid kinds borrow a rigged model, so they walk; the rest are shapes. Socket positions are in metres on the placeholder before it is scaled to the genius's height; 'bone' sockets ride the rig.",
